// A perfectly valid policy that a BOUNDED MODEL CHECKER cannot represent.
//
// Cedar's `Long` runs to 2^63-1, and a budget cap written in cents reaches nine figures without
// anyone thinking about it. TLC holds integers in a Java int and reserves `Integer.MAX_VALUE`, so
// the largest literal it will accept is 2147483646 -- measured, not assumed: 2147483646 checks and
// 2147483647 fails.
//
// WITHOUT AN EXPLICIT REFUSAL the failure arrives from inside TLC, as
//
//     Error: TLC can't handle a number this big.
//     3000000000
//
// from a run that names neither the policy nor the field, at a point where a reader has no reason
// to suspect the literal. This fixture exists so that stays a refusal naming the construct.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h AgentCore::Action::"approve_trade"::response{ }
    && context.input.amount_cents < 3000000000
};
